title: 'statement-store: keep blocking store calls off the async runtime'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Statement store calls that wait for the disk run on blocking threads: the validation workers,
    the maintenance task and both RPC submit methods. The gossip loop reads the admission
    watermark from an atomic counter. A store that waits for a slow disk no longer parks the
    threads of the shared runtime, so the node keeps importing blocks under statement overload.
    Nodes that build the statement handler themselves should spawn its validation executor with
    `spawn_blocking`.
crates:
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: patch
- name: sc-rpc-api
  bump: patch
- name: sc-rpc-spec-v2
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: patch
- name: staging-node-cli
  bump: patch
